  "description": "The 2026 Oregon gubernatorial election is a rematch between Democratic incumbent Tina Kotek and Republican state senator Christine Drazan, who also faced off in 2022 when Kotek won by less than 4 percentage points. Oregon has not elected a Republican governor since 1982, and this race will test whether the GOP can break that decades-long losing streak amid voter concerns over housing, homelessness, and cost of living. Kotek is seeking a second term after a first term marked by a homelessness state of emergency, a drug decriminalization rollback, and an early literacy initiative, while Drazan is campaigning on restoring accountability, cutting taxes, and improving public safety after serving as House Republican Leader and the 2022 GOP nominee. Early polling shows a competitive race, with one February poll giving Kotek a 5-point lead and a May survey showing the candidates tied at 45% each.",
