      "name": "Tina Kotek",
      "party": "Democratic",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Tina Kotek is the 39th governor of Oregon, first elected in 2022, and previously served as Speaker of the Oregon House of Representatives from 2013 to 2022, making her the longest-serving House Speaker in state history. She began her career as a policy advocate at the Oregon Food Bank and later as policy director at Children First for Oregon before being elected to the Oregon House in 2006. Kotek, an openly lesbian governor, has prioritized addressing homelessness, expanding summer learning programs, protecting abortion access, and reforming Oregon's drug laws during her tenure.",
