      "party": "Republican",
      "incumbent": false,
      "summary": "Christine Drazan is a Republican state senator from Oregon's 26th district, appointed in 2025, and previously served as House Republican Leader and a state representative from 2019 to 2022 and again in 2025. She was the Republican nominee for governor in 2022, losing to Tina Kotek by less than 4 percentage points. Drazan, a lifelong Oregonian from Klamath Falls, has built a reputation for using parliamentary tactics to block Democratic priorities such as cap-and-trade legislation and leading efforts to refer transportation taxes to voters.",
